>
>Strangely enough, there even DO exist desktop applications that run
>on VMS (though grossly out of line with pricing for the same class
>apps on a desktop running Wintel). Much COULD be fixed, provided
>the Powers that Be at DEC had the guts to fix them. Ending the
>"get the last nickel out of the suckers running VMS" mindset (where
>it still exists) is part of that. A 10 SPECmark workstation running
>VMS with a suite of apps ought to be costed at roughly what a similar
>workstation on Wintel would be, for starters. Factors of 1.2 or 1.5
>in cost of software could kinda be understood, I guess, but factors of
>10 or worse are mighty hard to live with.

