>that the Alpha chip will be out of production after the Intel 64 bit
>chip as been shipped, because the settlement are saying, that DEC will
>port the DEC unix and NT/alpha to the new chip.

The agreement says that Digital will port Digital Unix to IA64 (which makes
sense since it is one of the two 64-bit Unixes out there and SGI
did not make any announcements to this effect). The agreement does
*not* say that we are porting NT to it (you can't port NT/Alpha, that
is a software/hardware combination). The agreement *does* say that
Digital will build a range of IA64 *systems* (which presumably will
be able to run either NT/IA64 or Digital Unix/IA64). This is no different
from Digital building IA32 systems right now (which run NT/IA32 or
SCO Unix or whatever). Intel based products have been part of product
portfolio for a long time.

