The chip Samsung developed is 'EV-67', also known as 21264'A', i.e. one 
generation beyond the 0.35 um 21264 'EV-6' expected by DEC. The 700 MHz 
21264'A' should have performance in the region of 50 SPECint95 and 70 
SPECfp95 with an aggressive cache and mem subsystem. And it's 700+ MHz on 
just the first prototype without any particular process optimisations...

And yes, Samsung is the foundry to watch: don't forget Samsung played a 
key role in killing Intel in the DRAM market long ago, and with their 
aggressive marketing&pricing, advanced processes and no-compromise 
standing (not to forget ability to design their own Alpha derivatives), 
they're the one to make sure Alpha remains on the top even if Intel 
attempts to screw up 'their' Alpha manufacturing in the now-DEC fab. 
Everything develops as planned to bring the Alpha out as an 
industry-standard arch independent of DEC (about the time)...

And yes, count on 1 GHz+ with Kryotech cooling...

