In article <878144398.9907@dejanews.com>, p_sabotka@litle.net writes:
:I've recently acquired a VAXstation 3100/30 with VMS.  I would be
:interested in attaching an external SCSI CDrom to this system.	Will any
:SCSI CD-ROM work with this, or are there only specific external CDroms
:which will work with this system ?

  The CD-ROM drive must support 512 byte sectors -- the typical CD-ROM
  has 2048 byte sectors, but some third-party drives optionally support
  this sector size, and most (all?) DIGITAL CD-ROM drives support this.

	--

  Since you've recently acquired the VAXstation 3100, you will want to
  be aware that all members of the VAXstation 3100 series have a hard
  limit of 1.073 GB for the total size of the system disk -- disks that
  are larger might boot, but are not supported and are not recommended.
  The primitive boot driver in the VAXstation 3100 console PROM "wraps"
  sector references past 1.073 GB, and this can cause problems during
  system bootstraps and (worse) during system crashes.  Data disks can
  be larger -- prior to V6.0, the OpenVMS disk addressing limit is 8.5
  GB.  With V6.0 and later, the supported addressing limit is 1 TB.

  -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
