p_sabotka@litle.net writes:
> I've recently acquired a VAXstation 3100/30 with VMS.  I would be
> interested in attaching an external SCSI CDrom to this system.	Will any
> SCSI CD-ROM work with this, or are there only specific external CDroms
> which will work with this system ?

  Just about any drive should work (assuming it supports the set sector size
command) when the system is running. To be able to boot from the CD-ROM drive,
you'll need one that's configurable for 512 byte sectors (the default is 2048).

  You also need the screwball SCSI cable (68-pin HD male on the system) to
connect the drive. It's a BC56H-0x, where "x" is 3, 6, or 9 for 3, 6, or 9
feet.

