Well, Andrew, let me first say that yes, VMS HAS been hacked in the past.
I must say that more people are aware of security issues these days, but
in the past several methods were used to good results: social engineering,
insider knowledge (default passwords, etc), trojan horses, and even patches
to VMS intself.  yes, I..er...people have used these to gain access to
quite a few machines.
