in place for SYSTEST.  And at one time TELENET was a good hunting ground for
the intellectually curious hacker. (Notice I did not say *cracker*, for while
that was the end result, a true hacker was not out for maliciousness, but
rather intellectual stimulation.)

Oh, and I had a copy of VMS source on microfiche as long ago as 1984. It wasn't
all that hard to come by, tho buying my own reading machine raised a few
eyebrows.  In fact, the source for PHONE was quite amusing and opened up a
whole new potential for easedropping in on conversations.  I don't think PHONE
is used quite as much anymore, but we used to use it heavily back in college.

