In article 
    <0352F4714E497FD9.4AD1C8565433E6CA.B63C85BEC921EC2E@
       library-proxy.airnews.net>, "tim L." <"timled "@atlcom.net> writes:

> I am in need of another CISCE-AA. Does any one know of where I can get
> another pair. I have a 32 node (dual path)CI cluster, and I need to go
> to 48+ nodes,  Pls e-mail and/or post.

        I'm confused by your use of the term "dual path" above.  CI _is_
    dual path with separate transmit and  receive (for those who haven't
    seen  it,  that  means  _four_ cables from each  node  to  the  Star
    Coupler).  The last time I looked, a given CI "network" was  limited
    to  a  total  of  32 nodes, and at most 16 of them could be "hosts",
    i.e., VMS systems.

        Now since some VMS systems support more than one CI adapter, you
    may have those 16 (or fewer)  systems  on two (or more?) CI networks
    giving,  for example, 16 hosts access to 32 storage controllers.  Is
    this what you're after?  AFAIK, you cannot simple increase a 32-port
    Star Coupler to a 48-ports.  It's not  supported  and  probably  the
    software will complain or otherwise fail in nasty ways.  :-(

        But this brings up  another  question.   There  must be a lot of
    unused  Star  Couplers "out there".  Have you tried talking  to  the
    various used equipment  dealers?   I've  had  very  good  luck  with
    Midwest  Systems  (1-800-328-7000,  ask  for Tom Doty and tell him I
    sent you) and Great  Lakes  Computer  (1-619-940-3800, ask for Kathy
    Hutt and tell _her_ I sent you :-), but there are several others out
    there  as  well.   Depending  on the item, you  can  get  incredible
    deals...it's like used car dealers only better.  :-) :-)

        -Ken
