Are you seening the drive at the console prompt? On my DS3100 (just
starting to learn):

>> test -c
MEM: 
VIDEO:
ETHERNET STA ADDR:
SCSI DEVS:
U[7]			usually left empty
U[6]			usually the controller
U[5]
...
U[0]
should list all of the SCSI ID's (among other things) along with what
devices it sees attatched. If it sees the drive there, you probably
need to MAKEDEV the device in Ultrix (assuming that is what you are
using). Someone more familiar with UNIX can probably better help you
from here. I am a hardware person trying to teach myself UNIX
software. (I prefer VMS)

The SCSI ID's need to be set to different values, and different from
the controller (usually 6). The SCSI cable needs to be terminated at
the two ends, usually at the external port of the DS and on the
controller itself, so the internal drives should not need termination.
If the external terminator is different, or you have a different cable
than my DS3100, termination of the last drive on the bus may need to
be terminated.

Good Luck

Steve

