The Alpha architecture does not look like it's in trouble now, nor will
it be for some time to come. Without a new fab, it would be at risk
in a few years (I heard the existing fab 6 was designed for feature
size down to 0.18 u) since smaller features and Cu process will most
likely need new tooling. Given a 10 year deal with Intel to fab
things, this could be very good news; 10 years is "forever" in this
industry...

