Hey Larry!  Good comment, which took me reading through about 20 posts
to appreciate fully.  The success of the fabless approach really boils
down to time to market for these newer Alpha generations.  If Intel either
(1) fails to use it's best methods, or (2) fails to use it's best methods in
a timely fashion, then both Digital and Alpha are in deep deep trouble.
Since there is no incentive for Intel to do either of these things, one
would *hope* that Digital's lawyers were "smart enough" to write in both
process and schedule into the agreement.  I can't imagine Intel agreeing
to such a thing, but maybe.

