Sully,

The SCSI CD-ROM driver used for your Toshiba SCSI CD-ROM drive depends
on which SCSI host adapter you have in your system, not the brand name
of SCSI CD-ROM drive.

Typically, a SCSI system has an ASPI host manager driver in CONFIG.SYS
to establish a software interface to the hardware, then an ASPI CD-ROM
driver such as Adaptec's ASPICD.SYS.  Finally, like all DOS-level
CD-ROM drives, a SCSI drive needs MSCDEX.EXE in AUTOEXEC.BAT...

Ben Myers

