> Publisher, Shannon Knows DEC

What I question is whether anyone is doing the math to figure out what 
lack of reliability costs, both in downtime and in support dollars. So 
far I have not heard of anyone corporate who has actually compared the 
(long-term) cost of any two technologies, other than Gartner Group stuff 
about cost of ownership for PC vs. Mac.  I suspect that client/server in 
general is going to cost a buncha buncha bucks to support at anything 
near the reliability of some of our legacy systems.  I *know* that our 
VAXen have run & run & run with little or no care & feeding. If anyone 
has any hard numbers (or good stories) about relative cost of support, 
I'd be interested to hear them.  

Nora Narum
Using my own computer to voice my own thoughts on my own nickel.



