DEC makes a series 5 daughtercard for that configuration ?54-23534-06?. The
daughtercard is socketed for 2cpu's but the MLB will only support one CPU and
it must be the 5volt variety.  This configuration is identical to the Prioris
590 which is still supported upto 5200DP but you must buy the current MLB
(54-23984-01).  The cache is proprietary and expensive. Daughtercards are $120
to $240. The current MLB is $675.  Cache for the 5133 is <$70; For the 5200 I
was Quoted $449.
Current BIOS is 2.08 and works very nicely in both my 590 (old MLB) and in my
5133DP (new MLB).
Be sure to download the current SCU while you are there

