>But I don't know which one to go for.  Both are about the same price.  The
>SGI machine comes with a monitor but the Alpha does not.  

For number crunching: no.  The SGI will be much slower.  Most of the
comparisons you heard were for the current lineup.  The SGI above probably
has a more impressive graphics card while the Alpha has a more impressive
CPU.  A good Pentium Pro systems would probably be better than an R4600-133
for number crunching.

The R8000 and R10000 were SGIs first good number crunchers.

I wouldn't say the R4000SC/R4400 systems were bad for number crunching, but
not competitive with offerings from other vendors at the time.  Certainly
not competitive with current processors

If I was in your situation, I would only buy an SGI if my university had the
Varsity program and would include me in it.  Otherwise, it is like having
your own front-end loader.  Cool, but a bit expensive for general
gardening...
