In article <344D8549.7D37@storm.ca>, Stan Pietkiewicz <stanp@storm.ca> writes:
:I just acquired a MVax 3600 this past weekend, and my exploring it has 
:brought out a few questions:
:
:1)  On boot-up (every time), the firmware puts up the language menu. Is 
:this an indication that the nicads are dead, or is there a flag I can set 
:from the console to set and forget this?

  This is typical behaviour of a dead (or uncharged) nicad pack, or
  if the mode switch is set to "query".  The typical mode switch on
  this series has three positions: "normal" (arrow), "query" (face),
  and "test" (circle-T).

:2)  Does anyone have a manual for a KDA50 disk controller handy to look 
:up the jumper settings to set the board to an altermate address? I've got 
:one KDA50 in the box, and I'd like to add a second one. 

  I don't.

  There are a couple of MicroVAX-specific sites listed in the OpenVMS
  Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ).  You might want to check there.

  As a side-note, I'd tend to look for controllers other than the KDA50,
  as I'd prefer to use disks other than the RA-series.  (The RA-series
  disks are (were) good ones, but they're getting old, and they're big,
  power-hungry, and slow by current (no pun intended) standards.)

  For this particular sort of configuration, I'd tend to look for an
  HSD-series DSSI-to-SCSI adapter, and some SCSI disks.

:3)  Why would a KZQSA not show up when I type  >>> sh qbus   on the 
:console?? It responds (and recognizes disks) when it's in the DS5500 I've 
:got, and there doesn't seem to be an address conflict when it's in the 
:MVax..... it just doesn't show up :-{(. Jumper settings for this one 
:would be appreciated as well :-})

  Probably a misconfigured Q-bus, or a misconfigured KFQSA controller
  setting, or (more likely) both.

  Also note that KZQSA does not support magnetic disks under OpenVMS;
  only tapes and CD-ROMs are supported.

:4)  I've got a third-party SCSI controller ( CQD-260 from CMD Technology) 
:(I actually have the manual for this one!!) which the MVax recognizes, 
:but the CQD260 doesn't recognize any disks I attach to it. I haven't 
:tried connecting a differential drive, since I don't have one. Anything 
:special I need to do with this board?

  Donno.  If the controller correctly emulates a supported controller,
  then it should operate as expected when connected at the appropriate
  CSR and interrupt vector addresses.  (Note that adding or removing
  a Q-bus controller can and quite often does require changes to the
  CSR and interrupt vector settings on other controllers -- the Q-bus
  uses a "cascading" mechanism for assigning CSRs and vectors.)

:5)  What baud rates will a CXY-08 support? Will it support an external 
:modem?

  19.2 Kbaud and yes, respectively.  Some folks have reportedly gotten
  short and well-shielded serial line CXY08 configurations working at
  38.4 Kbaud, but I do not know if this speed is officially supported.

