In article <1997Oct24.163300.1@sldb4.slac.stanford.edu>, fairfield@sldb4.slac.stanford.edu writes:
:        Ask on comp.os.vms if you  want  to know how to _remove_ already
:    installed   DECNET/Plus   and  replace  it  with  DECNET   IV.    My
:    recollection of previous  postings  is  that  it's  easier  to  just
:    install  VMS  from  scratch,  without DECNET, then install DECNET IV
:    afterwards...


  It is usually easier to skip the installation of DECnet-Plus during
  the OpenVMS installation, but you can remove DECnet-Plus and install
  DECnet Phase IV.  To do so:

  Mount the distribution kit, then:

    $ PRODUCT REMOVE DECNET_OSI

  To see which products are dependent on which, use:

    $ PRODUCT SHOW PRODUCT/FULL

  To install DECnet Phase IV from CD-ROM:

    $ MOUNT/OVER=ID ddcu:
    $ PRODUCT INSTALL DECNET_PHASE_IV -
      /SOURCE=ddcu:[KITS.DECNET_PHASE_IV_KIT]

    ...where ddcu: is the name of the CD-ROM drive.

  To install DECnet Phase IV from TK50 tape:

    $ MOUNT/OVER=ID mmcu:
    $ PRODUCT INSTALL DECNET_PHASE_IV -
      /SOURCE=mmcu:

    ...where mmcu: is the device name of the tape drive.

  In the case of any product dependency on DECnet-Plus specific to the
  OpenVMS operating system itself, you can answer "no" to the "do you
  want to terminate?", though the OpenVMS reference will cause a future
  OpenVMS upgrade that "takes the defaults" to install DECnet-PLUS.  If
  you have products (other than OpenVMS itself) that are dependent on
  DECnet-Plus, you will need to resolve those dependencies individually.

  
