Hi.

We are using DEC COBOL Compiler Driver V2.4-863 on OSF1 V4.0 386 alpha.

Being a typical academic, I don't know much about cobol.  I am
assisting some of our students who are teaching it to themselves.  We
have encountered a problem which seems to be incorrect behavior of the
compiler or the run-time library.  The symptom is that when any
program tries to open a file, say "foo.dat", for input, it hangs for
about thirty seconds and then issues the message:

cobrtl: severe: Error during OPEN on file foo.dat

The file foo.dat exists and is readable by the user.  Any suggestions
as to what might be the problem will be very welcome.  Please e-mail
me responses since I do not normally read this group.

Here is a sample program that shows this problem.  It compiles without
warnings using the command ``cobol -warn all oneline.cob -o oneline''
It runs OK on a VAX/VMS system.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.

PROGRAM-ID.   oneline.
AUTHOR.       Robert Moniot
DATE-WRITTEN. October 1997.

*This is a simple program that reads the first line of a file and
*writes it to standard output.

ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
  FILE-CONTROL.
      SELECT INPUT-FILE ASSIGN TO "foo.dat".

DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.

FD    INPUT-FILE
      RECORD CONTAINS 80 CHARACTERS.
01    INPUT-FILE-RECORD                 PIC X(80).

WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
   77 INPUT-LINE PIC X(80).


PROCEDURE DIVISION.

EXECUTIVE-PARA.
       OPEN INPUT INPUT-FILE.
       READ INPUT-FILE RECORD INTO INPUT-LINE AT END STOP RUN.
       DISPLAY INPUT-LINE.
       CLOSE INPUT-FILE.
       STOP RUN.

