We have a couple of GIGASWitch/ATM switches, v2.0 linecards.

The current sw level 2.1.x works with the default 8M memory,
but under certain extreme conditions there is not much to 
spare.

So we decided to get more memory, and bought PCP7M-AC laptop memory
through official digital channels as the tables suggest, we even
told them that they are for the ATMswitches. 

We installed one SO-DIMM to a test switch.

The #�%&/ ATM switch just blinked one led, and did not even start 
boot procedures. We tried with another DIMM and another line card,
same result.

So we returned the pile of memory upgrades, and asked again. This
time they used code DAGME-AB for the upgrade, and the price was
considerably higher. Today we received three expensive 16M DIMMs,
which worked.

The only problem is that also these DIMMs carry the laptop memory
code PCP7M-AC.

The GIGA has MIPS, PCs have Intel. Could it be some kind of processor
specific refresh/whatever difference ? (and we could get the memory
cheaper if we would just know which memory chips we need ;-)

These working DIMMs have MCM517400CT60 chips.

