ali@iriquois.eel.ufl.edu (Ali Anghaie) writes:

I totaly agree,

For my part, IRIX 6 OS realy better than Solaris. My IRIX 6.4 machines
had never crashed, and the admin tools are realy simple to use and powerfull.
More over, of admin files are standard and vi-able.

Solaris is really buggy. Kernel panics are rare, but cores are dumped dayly.
 - passwd dumps core if root cred had problems
 - chooser dumps core if HP UX odl xdm responds
 - mountd dumps core if a commer is missing in netgroups
 - dbx dumps core in debugging some cores. (your core then is deleted...)
 - .... there are tousand of sun commands which dumps core.
 Solaris 2.5.1 (whith all recommanded patches) is a core generator.
SAF is a ..... well there is no name to describe that thing.
When installing an hp jet printer, the pmadm command are not issued.
In order to create the ports, you have to create a dummy printer with
admintool and delet it. (the port is created but never deleted).
And so on....

Under IRIX, everything works immediately! and installing recommanded
patch is not hazardous.

The only thing I'd like to see standard in IRIX is ONC and IDO which
are options that you always need.



