SKD'S TOP TEN REASONS TO DO DECUS ANAHEIM

(c) 1997 by Terry C. Shannon, Publisher, Shannon Knows DEC

It�s less than a week until DECUS Anaheim �97, The Event Formerly Known
as the DECUS US Chapter Symposium and Trade Show, gets underway at the
Anaheim Convention Center. SKD�s editor will occupy his usual cheap digs
in Anaheim from November 1 though 6 to partake of his 28th consecutive
DECUS US symposium. Assessing the mood of the user community and getting
the facts on products announced and unannounced is part and parcel of my
job, but to paraphrase the Navy, DECUS isn't just a job, it's an
adventure. 

Although the 20th anniversary of the VAX architecture and the VMS
operating system portends VMS-centricity at the Anaheim get-together,
the Fall '97 event promises to be an interesting symposium for one and
all. And there may be a few surprises: The Rumourmonger Formerly Known
as Charlie Matco is rumoured to be planning a foray into the VMS
campground, and SKD can neither confirm nor deny the existence of a
limited, numbered edition of a periodical cryptically entitled MATCO
Knows DEC. (But if it did exist, it would be a collector's item...)

If the prospect of seeing a rumourmonger rise from the grave--or mayhap
even the sight of a TurboLaser running OpenVMS, DUNIX and WNT
concurrently--isn't enough to whet your appetite, herewith are SKD's Top
Ten reasons why you should line up, sign up, and enlist as a DECUS
attendee today.

10) Eschew the smog and the shakes in low-ozone, fault-tolerant Anaheim. 

9) Add some luster--and perhaps a few extra nodes--to your TruCluster by
plumbing the depths of Digital UNIX 4.0D, the latest and greatest
release of a bulletproof 64-bit Unix implementation.

8) JUST SAY NO to absinthe recipes on the 'net! Get the True Facts on
the personal side of the Internet by attending The Human Side of the
Internet: May We Play at Work, Please?, Net author Diane Reiner's talk
on curricular and, well, extracurricular Internet activities.

7) Take a trip down memory lane by participating in the OpenVMS 20th
Anniversary bash, the VAX/OVMS 20th Anniversary Pioneers Roundtable, and
the VAX/VMS 20th Anniversary Trivia Bowl. While you�re at it, check out
the past, present, and future of the bulletproof OS at the OpenVMS
Campground.

6) Learn why Network the Dog is barking up the wrong tree. The Cluster
is the System, and OpenVMS Galaxy architects will tell you why, as they
begin to make Galaxy a household word.

5) Scarf up the latest information--not to mention some really swell
trade show graft and giveaways--from Digital, its partners, ISVs, and
third-party ironmongers at the DECUS Trade Show.

4) Pig out on mongo meals 24 hours per day at the world-renowned
Belisle�s Restaurant, located just down the road from the Anaheim
Convention Center.

3) Arm yourself with cool codenames and questions for the Digital
Listens panel by attending SKD's ever-popular and historically
dead-accurate Digital's Strategic Directions session just before the
Vice Presidential Inquisition.

2) Get second, third and fourth opinions on DEC's future directions from
symposium keynoter and DEC Marketing Czar Bruce Claflin (Digital's
Strategy and Direction), and VPs Jesse Lipcon (Digital's Hardware
Direction) and Wes Melling (Digital's Software Direction).

1) And the Number One reason to attend DECUS Anaheim '97: Anaheim isn't
Las Vegas and DECUS isn't Comdex. Which is probably just as well!

There you have 'em: ten sure-fire reasons to spend the first week of
November in Anaheim. Now is the time to do the Right Thing: call
1-800-DECUS55 or drop by the DECUS website at www. decus.org to register
for DECUS Anaheim �97.



