In article <EIKtH7.JyK@nonexistent.com>, 
    		Ray Badiak <rmbadiak@blast.net> writes:
> Phase4 on Alphas
> 
> We are planning to replace 2 VAX 4000/500's
> with 2 AlphaServer 800's. This network also
> has 9 DecRouter250's. Anyone know if the 250's
> will work with the OSI DecNet. Can we keep
> Phase4 instead. Do we loose anything by staying
> with Phase4. I appreciate your comments.

        Yes, you  _can_  stay  with  DECNET  Phase  IV  under  VMS  7.1.
    However,  given that your AS800's will probably arrive with  factory
    installed software already in place, they'll probably (or  at  least
    _may_)  have  DECNET/Plus (the latest name for DECNET Phase V/DECNET
    OSI), and you may want  to  do  a  fresh  install  of the O/S to the
    Alpha's system disk.  If you _do_ reinstall the O/S, the trick (with
    VMS  7.1) is to answer NO to the question asking whether to  install
    DECNET, then when you're done, install DECNET IV (as you  would  any
    other  layered  product) using VMSINSTAL (unless it's a PCSI package
    now).  The savesets are in a subdirectory of the VMS O/S CDROM.

        Ask on comp.os.vms if you  want  to know how to _remove_ already
    installed   DECNET/Plus   and  replace  it  with  DECNET   IV.    My
    recollection of previous  postings  is  that  it's  easier  to  just
    install  VMS  from  scratch,  without DECNET, then install DECNET IV
    afterwards...

        -Ken
