:What kind of disks do they take?

  By "cabinet", I'll assume this is the BA123 "coffee table on rollers"
  enclosure, also known as the "world box", and not the BA23 "space heater"
  pedestal enclosure.  (As in "I dropped your space heater", a phrase that
  one of the house movers said to me nearly a decade back.  I can :-) now.)

  Without information on which controller is connected to those connectors
  and where you are seeing those connectors in the BA123 box, I'll guess 
  that these connectors are an RQDX3 controller bulkhead, which supports
  the RD5x series disks, with the RD54 being the most recent (some would
  say "last") and largest (circa 159 MB) of that series of disks.

  Rather than describing connectors to us, it would be best to describe
  the controller(s) present in the Q-bus -- the DIGITAL Q-bus cards
  usually have a letter-and-digits code stamped on the spine or handles,
  an example would be the M7606 stamped on the MicroVAX II KA630 CPU
  module.  From these, we can usually tell you what your configuration
  is, and what sort of disks or tapes can be supported.

