Are you sure about the "dec435"? If it is a DE435, then it is
a PCI card. The DE425 is an EISA version, but you still need
to check whether there are Alpha versions of the driver(s) and
possible EISA configuration overlay files as Intel versions 
won't work (look at the Microsoft Windows NT Hardware 
Compatibility List, HCL for supposedly certified EISA boards 
with Alpha drivers, or check the vendor for their latest drivers 
as it might not be on the HCL list, but still work).

See

    http://www.microsoft.com/hwtest/hcl/

for the HCL (FWIW, the DE425 doesn't seem to be on the list ;-),
and

    http://www.networks.digital.com/dr/nics/drivers/

for the latest drivers for Digital Ethernet adapters.

