Glenn A. Laguna wrote:
> For my money, an Alpha running Linux is the way to go.

If he wants a number cruncher, then don't run Linux on an Alpha.

gcc 2.7.* is weak in key areas of optimization (instruction scheduling and
alias analysis in particular), and this hurts the performance of Alpha/Linux
apps quite badly (by as much as a factor of 2 in some cases). The Alpha/Linux
team is very aware of this problem, and the egcs project is working to
improve gcc's optimization abilities, but egcs is still very much in beta
testing at the moment.

Using DEC's compilers running on Digital UNIX, OpenVMS or even Windows NT
will give much better "number crunching" performance.


