> > The first thing I recommend is watching your capitalization. Just to be

> Why should one match to the capitalization in the examples given by
> the designers of one particular search engine?

First: As with browsers, you should take care to work with all major
search engines, and therefore you should look at all these search
engines' descriptions.

Second, matching the capitalization in the examles avoids unwanted
side effects. For instance, several search engines have a rule like
- keywords written in all-lower-caps will be delivered in
  case-insensitive searches,
- keywords containing at least one upper-case char will be delivered
  only in case-sensitively correct searches.

> But I'd expect any decent search engine to treat values of the NAME attribute
> of a META element as _case-insensitive_. If search engines don't work
> that way, there is little we can do unless at least the most popular
> engines explicitly reveal how they want the cases to be.

