>3. SGI's are the most highly recommended machines.

Locally, we provide second-level consultation support for Sun SunOS,
Sun Solaris, SGI IRIX, DEC Ultrix, and Digital Unix for the
University.  I, for whatever reason (mainly related to ease of use and
consequent reduction in call volume :-), tend to favor SGIs if they're
to be dropped on a Unix neophytes desk.  We seem to have far fewer
calls and problems/questions from the less Unix saavy users for SGI
machines than some of the other vendors hardware. I notice that my
colleague here in the support group seems to also tend to like SGIs
from the (relative) ease of support perspective as well (SGI does have
its' problems though and dealing with the SGI "corporate folks" can be
a bit maddening at times -- the SGI engineers have all been
pretty helpful in my experience and newsgroup support by those folks is
probably the best of any vendor). If someone wants a "graphics"
machine, almost invariably we end up mentioning SGIs.

>4. Sun Sparc's are not such a good machine.  Alpha's are better than
