In article <105FADF85F25D1118F3300A02461FAC33EBAB1@PIONEER>, "Perkins, Edwin" <eperkins@bev.etn.com> writes:
>
>I have a DEC3000 Model 500 and the built in video has died.  The
>remainder of the system still works fine.  Does anyone know how to
>configure the console to work from a serial port?

Look on the back panel in line with the video connector.  There
are two switches.  One is the "S3" switch, which changes the
system from video console to serial line console.  I believe it's
the smaller of the two switches. Then repower/reboot.

(This is a good reason for keeping the hardware manuals that
come with the system: it includes instructions on how to
do this, with illustrations.)

