>
>I found a 175 MHz Octaine (64 MB RAM) to be considerably faster
>(50-100%) with some floating point/memory thoughput intensive finite
>elements simulation (written mostly in Fortran) than a 200 MHz
>UltraSparc (128 MB RAM). Honestly, I'm quite puzzled why 

Memory bandwidth on the Octane is considerably higher than on 
the 200 MHz UltraSparc systems.  This is an O(1) effect for 
certain classes of finite element codes, especially if using 
low-order elements and/or conjugate-gradient equation solvers.

Older SGI machines were quite a bit poorer in this regard, which
probably explains why you saw weak results on Indigo2 systems.

See http://www.cs.virginia.edu/stream/ for numbers....
