Ray <ray@cult.ray.org> wrote:
> I have some problems getting a DECstation 5000/300 running. I'm trying to use
> the DEC VR260 Monitor which works fine for my VAXstation and my DECstation
> 2100, but with an a bit different cable, that also supplies connectors for
> keyboard and mouse, which seems to be designed for the DECstation 5000.

[snip]

> labled PMAG-B, I have no idea what that is) that disables the normal
> monitor outlet? Or does anybody have any other idea, why I can't see anything.

The 5000 series DECstation (and maybe the Personal DECstations) have a
console cable that splits out the keyboard and mouse, and have a separate
cable that connects the frame-buffer to the monitor.

The 2100/3100 DEC/VAXstations have an integrated framebuffer connector
on the mainboard and separate connectors for keyboard and mouse.

The two part numbers I have on my cables are:

	17-02640-01 (console) 
	BC26G-09 (video)

Good luck.  (if all else fails pull the framebuffer and 9600n81 to port 3)

