>The optimal translations vary widely
>with the target architecture, and the first three constructs
>have been discussed many times in this newsgroup,
>yet the language designers decline to standardize the constructs.

Not all of these constructs, and not all language designers.

Lisp has your truncated base-2 logarithm, population count, and
greatest common divisor.  It doesn't need MULLO/MULHI.

LIA-2 includes GCD, MULLO, and MULHI, and it is supposed to be
"language-independent", in the sense that language standardisers
will be expected to provide standard bindings to it.

-- 
