> Well, there are a lot of specifics, but this mornings SF newspaper has
> Warner Bros selling a ton of SGI systems.  Why?  I'd like to know.  But
> probably not because they are great number crunchers.

I found a 175 MHz Octaine (64 MB RAM) to be considerably faster
(50-100%) with some floating point/memory thoughput intensive finite
elements simulation (written mostly in Fortran) than a 200 MHz
UltraSparc (128 MB RAM). Honestly, I'm quite puzzled why (I tried to use
the best machine specific optimization on both machines).
On the other hand, older SGIs such as Indigos or Indies are poor number
crunchers in my experience, even considering their age (but they are
still nice graphics terminals).


