Hi Guys:

I have a question re: backups using dump/vdump. 
We have two DEC alphas, one has all the UFS file systems andthe other
has all the AdVFS. To keep things simpler, we are using 'vdump' command
to backup the file systems on both machines. I understand that we can
perform a 'vdump 0' on the AdVFS while the users are still logged on.
But can we do the same thing on UFS?(i.e. perform 'vdump 0' on UFS in
multi-user mode). 

Another question: Can we run fsck command while the users are logged on
the system? Basically, what I am thinking of doing is to just check the
file systems (using fsck), and if everything looks good, then perform a
'vdump 0' in multi-user mode. Right now we shut the system down in
single-user to perform backups.

Another question: The System Adminsitration manual says that in UFS if a
dump 0 is performed in multi-user mode, and somebody is changing a file,
then the backup could be corrupt. Now my question is that 'Is the whole
backup bad or just the backup of that file.? (i.e. can we still use the
tape to restore other files if needed). 

thanks.

