In article <34453524.97EB5EF8@actgate.com>, Howard Taylor <taylor@actgate.com> writes:
:...have found a box that is labeled a DEC DEREP...
:...I assume this is just an ethernet repeater.

  Correct.

:...used to increase the length of an AUI cable???

  Incorrect.

  The DEREP and similar devices are used to retransmit all LAN traffic
  between two LAN segments.

  The slide-lock AUI connectors on the DEREP are used to connect to the
  transceivers; these transceivers are connected to the LAN segments.

  Many networks are now using bridges and brouters rather than repeaters,
  though there are definitely situations where repeaters can be useful.
  
