I would. I gather there are a few "vintage" boxes in private homes
here and there. There's an 11/780 in someones kitchen (England I
think) and a few PDP 11's around too.

I ran a VAX 6310  (64mb) and a HSC50 (CI Bus) at home for a year or
so, interestingly, the 6310 only drew about 2 amps from a 240vac wall
socket once I modded the 3 phase supply to work off single phase.
(It takes six people, a solid steel handcart and a station wagon or
utility to move/lift it by the way, done it that way twice now)
Amazing what a carton of West End Draught can accomplish :)
The HSC also modded for 240ac single phase, draws 2.5 amps. 
Ran 3 RA72's and an RA70 on it, & 2 x 4mm DAT, with VMS 6.
All up about 6 amps.
Wouldn't want to run it continuously at home, perhaps, but it's not
that bad. (There are 3 pcs at my house that are on virtually 24hrs a
day as it is)
Still in mothballs I have this stuff:
1 VAX 7580 (unmodded) with CI cabinet, minus the console cable, and
the console HDD is u/s. another HSC (minus most of it's channel cards)
TA78/TU78 Dual 1/2" Tape drive, (forklift for that one!) - minus 2 of
its 5v supplies, otherwise functional.  Oh and miles of 1/2" tapes
plus a 7 or 8 RA81's and a couple of RA82's. Phew.  In short a
complete cluster. It was going to wind up as razor blades unless I
took it. (Free, but on the condition that I took ALL of it)
Might resurrect the TA78 one day if I can get a couple of new psus.
No plans for the rest, except as spares. Unless someone has a console
HDD and console to computer cable for a 7580 going begging? Then who
knows?  I think there is a BSD variant it can run ok. 

(The 6310 is now "back at work" as a web/ftp/mail server at my current
employer, with another 4 RA70's tacked on as well. When they
eventually change to something else, I will probably take it home
again)
Theres a recent pic of it 'in situ' at www.stmarks.pp.catholic.edu.au

Yeah, I know, I'm nuts, but it was fun making it go, I had to really,
because I kept getting told it couldn't be done. I hate that. :)

