I don't mean to burst your bubble, but the graphics adapter that you
specified will not work in an Alpha system.  Alphas use a PCI bus, AGP is an
x86 thing.  Also, ISA is not something widely available on most Alpha
motherboards I have heard of, and when they are available there are usually
only 2 slots at most.  In addition I highly doubt that Creative Labs has
AlphaNT drivers for the AWE64, and you could do better (unless it is
strictly for games).  I won't even propose you expect to find CL supporting
it under UNIX or Linux.  Also, I am guessing this system is meant to be a
general-use/games system from the configuration.  Make sure that the games,
etc. that you want to run are Alpha friendly, through FX!32, native, or
otherwise.




