dwayne tillotson wrote:
> 
> A friend has an old DEClaser 1100 that they want to use on a new system. It
> looks like it is set up to run on a serial port. I would like to run it on
> a regular printer port. My friend does not have the manual and I haven't
> been able to get one from Digital. Any ideas?
> 
> Please email me directly as I don't read this newsgroup....
> 
> dwaynet@iname.com

Dwayne,

To select the parallel port do the following:

1) Take the printer offline.
2) Press the menu key.
3) Press the right or left arrow key until "interface" is on the left
of the readout.
4) Press the down arrow key, it will say "if".
5) Press the down arrow key, it will say "rs232c".
6) Press the right arrow key, it will say "centro".
7) Press the enter key.
8) Press the up arrow key twice, it will say "interface".
9) Press the right or left arrow key until "save nvram" is on the
left of the readout.
10) Press the enter key, it will say "ok".
11) Place the printer back on line.


Randy



