> 
> Mike. (Learning even more about Fortran every day.)

But if gcc knows the same amount of information as Fortran (i.e. that
f() is side-effect-free) it can also make the same optimisation. viz:

extern int f(int a) __attribute__ ((const));

int b(int a)
{
    return 0 * f(a);
}

becomes (since you are at ARM):

