Never tried the backup program but I have a different aproach, before
I install anything in win95 I run the batch file below:
(I have a c:/backup directory)

====
attrib c:\windows\user.dat -r -s -h
attrib c:\windows\user.da0 -r -s -h
attrib c:\windows\system.dat -r -s -h
attrib c:\windows\system.da0 -r -s -h

copy c:\windows\user.dat c:\backup\user.dat
copy c:\windows\user.da0 c:\backup\user.da0
copy c:\windows\system.dat c:\backup\system.dat
copy c:\windows\system.da0 c:\backup\system.da0
copy c:\windows\system.ini c:\backup\system.ini
copy c:\windows\win.ini c:\backup\win.ini

attrib c:\windows\user.dat +r +s +h
attrib c:\windows\user.da0 +r +s +h
attrib c:\windows\system.dat +r +s +h
attrib c:\windows\system.da0 +r +s +h
====

After I install and if I find I don't want to keep this program, I
uninstall it using the regular method from control panel and then I
run this restore batch file from the dos prompt (in dos mode, not in a
win95 window)

====
attrib c:\windows\user.dat -r -s -h
attrib c:\windows\user.da0 -r -s -h
attrib c:\windows\system.dat -r -s -h
attrib c:\windows\system.da0 -r -s -h

copy c:\backup\user.dat c:\windows\user.dat
copy c:\backup\user.da0 c:\windows\user.da0
copy c:\backup\system.dat c:\windows\system.dat
copy c:\backup\system.da0 c:\windows\system.da0
copy c:\backup\system.ini c:\windows\system.ini
copy c:\backup\win.ini c:\windows\win.ini

attrib c:\windows\user.dat +r +s +h
attrib c:\windows\user.da0 +r +s +h
attrib c:\windows\system.dat +r +s +h
attrib c:\windows\system.da0 +r +s +h
====

And with all the shareware I try this has done a pretty good job in
keeping me out of trouble, of course that was back when I only used
win95, now I mostly use NT..

Now if you do this before you run your backup program the system files
will be in the backup directory and they will be backed up, then after
a restore you can just go to the dos prompt and run the restore batch
and you'll be completely back to the point of that backup job. 
(maybe :)

