Are we talking about availability or reliability?  The two are similar in
concept and
often closely related, but there are differences.

>I've been running NT 3.51 on three 2100 4/275 and two 255/300 boxes since
>September, 1997 with out a problem.  Upgraded two of the boxes to NT 4.0 a
>couple of weeks ago and haven't had a problem.  I am looking to taking the
>other two to NT 4.0 in the next two weeks.  As far as staying up and
>functioning NT on Alpha is rock solid.]


We you able to do this upgrade without downtime?

Didn't think so.  With a VMScluster, it is easy to configure the hardware
and software
so that upgrades can be done without down time.  And hardware upgrades
and hardware repairs, too.  And its even possible to suffer from hardware
and software
failures without suffering downtime since most failures affect only one node
in a cluster.

Unix and NT clustering require that the apps be configured to work in the
failover
environment, but the interesting apps can't currently be supported.

The unfortunate reality is that certain interesting apps, eg., Exchange
Server,
aren't supported on OpenVMS.




