Hello,

I'm currently working on a space-efficient scheduler that can be used in any
lightweight threads library. To test it out, I'm looking for real, parallel,
multithreaded programs intended for shared memory (SMP) platforms. The
programs need to be written using a lightweight threads library (such as
pthreads), they should dynamically create and destroy threads, and preferably
perform dynamic memory (de)allocation. A number of scientific or database
applications may fall into this category. If you know of any such programs
with publicly available source code, please let me know! Please cc any
replies to me.

