> telephone numbers? 
> If you were one of them would you want me to post them on usenet?

Without details, it's impossible for anyone to comment on your friends or
colleagues. But I can say that I paid for my entire college education (up
to PhD) with essentially no support from my parents (they _did_ pay the
$50 enrollment fee, but that was about it). I worked while I was in school
and borrowed money. I don't think I'm that exceptional.

> 
> >I believe that the part
> >you disagree with is that the present system may require the beneficiary
> >pay back directly to society, in terms of loan repayments, their support
> >for their education. You apparently much prefer a situation where
> >everybody else pay for your entitlement.
> >
> 
> I'm too old to go back to school so this isn't personal. As for who
> pays what see above, your way is more expensive to society for sure.

I don't think you've provided any evidence of that.

