As I reported in the May 13 Shannon Knows DEC, a technology
cross-licensing agreement is a likely outcome of the Current
Unpleasantness. The outright SALE of Alpha almost certainly
is not.

Note that Intel had the opportunity to license Alpha way back in '91.
They chose not to do.

All of which beggars a question: if, as Intel claimed at the processor
"announcement" over three years ago, Merced is "better than Alpha," why
would Intel even want to bother with DEC's architecture.

