Andrew Cruickshank wrote:
> 
> The compilers keep a database of precompiled header information
> for each source file in a project. If you change the include files
> or add definitions ahead of the include files then this is detected
> and the precompiled header information is regenerated by the
> compiler/preprocessor.

"Precompiled headers" is really a misnomer. It's really a symbol
table cache. One of its somewhat counter-intuitive
characteristics is that it's more efficient, in a multi-module
program, to include the same set of headers in every module,
rather than try to figure out the minimum set needed by each
individual module. But I never liked doing that anyway...

-- 

