> I have a Celebris XL 590 (Dual Cpu module) currently with an Intel P90. 
> The question is can it be upgraded to the Intel P180MMX Overdrive chip ??

Nope.

The chipset on the daughterboard for the Celebris XL 590 doesn't support
MMX.
The best you can do "by the book" with that daughterboard is dual P5-133s.
"Should" be able to run dual non-MMX overdrives, but I haven't heard of
anyone trying it. DEC did make a P6 daughterboard for the Celebris XL.


My Celebris XL started as a 590 went to a 5133DP and now it's almost a 6150
(took it to DEC support June 27th, got a temp fix in Sept., hope to have
the repair completed before 1998).


Scott V



