If memory serves, the backplanes are:


H9270       4-slot Q22/Q22
                   Supports 4 Quads or 4 Duals.

H9273       9-slot Q18/CD
                  Supports 9 Quads or 9 Duals

H9275       9-slot Q22/Q22 with built-in termination.
                  Supports 9 Quads or 18 Duals

H9276       9-slot Q22/CD on first 3 slots and Q22/Q22 on the last 6 slots.
                  Supports 3 Quads or 3 Duals in Slots 1-3
                  Supports 6 Quads or 12 Duals in Slots 4-9
                  (Similar to the BA23 backplane, but has one more slot!)


Note that if you have ANY two-board sets that use the CD interconnect
(The RLV11 is the only one that pops to mind), you *MUST use the
H9273 backplane.

(Well, if you were running an 11/53 or an 11/93 with no additional
 memory, you *COULD* get  away with using an H9276, and putting
the RLV11 into slots 2 and 3, but that's another story. . .)

Also, if you are using the QUAD variety of 11/73 or 11/83, you DO NOT
want to use an H9275.  You MIGHT blow up your board.  Or your PMI
memory. . . .


Tim






