>me some dimensionality of the cache (or other) memory that
>I can actually take advantage of at the assembly level, then

Some architectures already offer some instructions to touch 
caches. PPC allows "zero cache line with no memory read"  and
load-register-bypass-cache.  I'd like to see some 
"write cache-line for vaddr1 to memory vaddr2 " etc.
Also it would be nice to see some more imagination in  virtual
addressing so that linked lists could be combined into virtual
flat arrays conveniently.

>Alas! I fear that this is all a matter of semantics, and
>the usual cyber-babble that computer scientists are prone to
>sprout.

Another bitter physicist, I presume.  Sorry  that the cold war ended, 
but there's nothing I can do.


