Sergio Rotstein wrote:
> 
> I suspect that this is probably not the best newsgroup to post this in
> but I hope somebody can guide me towards the proper resources...
> 
> I am trying to set up an alpha running openVMS (7.x) so that it will
> automatically perform a backup of a certain group of directories every
> day (full backup on Sundays, incremental backup the rest of the week).
> 
> Can anybody give me some pointers on how to go about this?

how about this:

Write a dcl procedure that submits itself to the batch queue to run on
each day at the desired hour  ...SUBMIT/AFTER=TOMORROW+"01:00" for
example to run at 1:00 am

At the beginning of the procedure, DAY = F$CVTIME("",,"WEEKDAY")

DAY will then be MONDAY, TUESDAY, ...etc.

Use the DAY symbol to do the backup you want to do .

Here's a quick example.  You change the particulars:

$! DAILY_BU.COM - Perform daily backups
$!
$! First, resubmit myself
$!
$ SBMIT/LOG=DAILY_BU.LOG/NONOTIFY/NOPRINT -
  /NAME=BACKUP/AFTER=TOMORROW+"00:00" DAILY_BU.COM
$!
$! Now get today's day of the week
$!
$ DAY = F$CVTIME("",,"WEEKDAY")
$!
$! Then do the proper backup based on the d-o-t-w
$!
IF DAY .EQS. "SUNDAY"
THEN
   BACKUP/IMAGE/RECORD/...
ELSE
   BACKUP/SINCE=BACKUP/RECORD/...
ENDIF
$!
$! All done
$!
$ EXIT


Don't forget the /RECORD qualifier on the backup command so you'll mark
the files for the incremental backups.

Steve

