This is a black & white (grayscale?) X terminal, circa 1990-1991.  The VT1300
was the color version.  I had a VT1200 back then.  If memory serves me correctly
you could have up to 3 or 4MB of memory on it.  It had some native fonts in ROM
or it could use a font server.  It also had a native window manager or you could
use a host based window manager.  Communcation was via LAT, TCP/IP, or
Decnet.

I don't recall what monitor came with it.



