Not sure which graphics subsystem is in your 450D2, but VGA.DRV is the
most basic graphics driver for Windows.  640 x 480 resolution and 16
colors.

You're running Windows 3.1 or Windows 95?  For Windows 3.1, I'd
suggest visiting DEC's web site and downloading the latest graphics
drivers for your EXACT model of computer.  If the graphics on your
system has enough memory, you should be able to run 640 x 480 @ 256
colors simply by installing the right software driver.

Windows 3.1 also has a fairly generic Super VGA driver for 640 x 480 @
256 colors.  You might simply click the Windows Setup icon, choose
Change System Settings and scroll thru the choices of graphics
drivers.  Be prepared to insert one of the original Windows 3.1
diskettes.

For Windows 95, it's Add Hardware should auto-detect the type of card
and install the right driver from the Win 95 CD-ROM.  But I'll guess
that you're still on Win 3.1... Ben Myers

