> easily generate a live mutant motherboard industry, as long as they don't
> fragment into more than one non-Intel socket/slot spec at a time.

It's not that hard, apparently.  I've heard Micron has its own Samurai
chipset which implements the 66 MHz PCI bus.  AMD is coming out with the
AMD-640 chipset (I think that's the name of it), and most likely they've
got other chipsets in the works.  Plus, who knows what will come out of
the little-known Asian companies in the near future?

Intel may be on top, but competition really isn't that far behind, in my
opinion.

