>>         |    ^    |
>>         V    |    V
>>     <-  Q    Q <- Q   CD <-CD <-CD
>
>I have a MicrovaxIII in a BA23. According to your drawing, it's
>completly OK, if the third slot (from the top) has only one 
>dual-height card (a DEQNA) in it? Or... does it need a grant card?
>My card layout is:
>         Q        Q        C        D
>	------------------------------
>                   KA 650-A
>                   memory card
>           deqna            (empty)
>         emulex?(u.q.o.)    emulex async multipl.
>           rqdx3            (finish)
>
>u.q.o.=unidentifiable qbus object; some Emulex ESDI HD/floppy controller
>Now, I don't know if the system sees the HD... It doesn't display
>anything on that... It tries to boot from the Ethernet adapter, and when
>I try >>> b dua0 (and likes), it says: "DEVOFFLN". 

The empty slot is fine.  The RQDX3 is in the wrong place -- move it
to the CD half of that slot.  If the RQDX3 controls DUA0, it won't be
getting the bus grants, which could explain the device offline error
on booting.  

If the emulex controller is the boot controller, try popping the RQDX3
out completely -- probably pay to pop the async mux out too to get a
minimal system.  You also want to check if the CSR & vector on the card
is set right -- do you have the manuals?  The way DEC do these is that
the OS & boot ROMs expect things to be at certain CSRs & vectors, and if
they aren't, the device doesn't get found.

