Do tell..  'Charity' refers to 'an act of good will or affection' or 'a
voluntary giving of money or other help to those in need.'  (these are strict
dictionary definitions, which I realize may not be precise enough in
philosophical circles, so if you have any refinements of terminology, I'd be
interested to hear).  If you can explain how having money taken from you under
threat of imprisonment or worse is an 'act of good will' or that the internal
revenue 'service' pilfering your money is 'voluntary', I'd like to know.

>Premiss: We want to offer every person an equal chance for education and
>a wealthy life.

Like it or not, that's an impossible premise to achieve by any system.  Though I
recognize its intrinsic appeal, to try to truthfully achieve it would be only
possible by bringing down those who accel.  People have varying levels of
physical fitness, mental acuity, etc. (even if you wish to limit yourself only
to the hereditary), and the fact of the matter is that perfect opportunity isn't
there for everyone to be whatever they want, no matter what.  To attempt it
would require handicapping everyone of ability in an area to bring them down to
'equality'.  I recognize people as rational beings who can interact and attempt
to further their lives by any means other than using force or deception against
the person or property of others, whatever their intrinsic abilities. 


