<helbing@monet.cs.uni-magdeburg.de.no_spam> wrote:

>syserror@micro-net.com (Aaron Bilger) writes:
>
>> Taxation is an arbitrarily applied, assigned an arbitrary numerical
>> amount by a government with no accountability, no restraint on being
>> able to increase how much it takes on a whim.
>
>So maybe that's the U.S. system then.  In a democracy, however, there
>is a choice.

'Democracy' is often used in a far too glorified sense.  In a complete democracy
51% of the people could vote to kill the other 49%.  I'm for individual rights,
not the mob rule of pure democracy.  Just because a majority of people vote to
take others' property or lives does not in any way make it right. 

>The same kind of choice you talk about in numerous
>postings when it comes to software. 

They are far different.  If I choose software from a company, be it Microsoft,
Netscape, or whatever, there is a known amount of money going voluntarily to the
company in exchange for known products and services.  With the government, it's
just not analogous, they choose how much you have to give, they choose what, if
any, will be spent and result in any indirect benefit to you.   Microsoft and
Netscape can't come and take my property, even if they were to set up an
arbitrary phone number or web address I could access and cast my 'vote' on how
much they take and then claim that this justified their theft.  Think about how
you would actually have to word a license agreement or contract to describe what
the government does, and whether this would really be anywhere near analogous to
any honest business in existence.  I've appended such a contract which would be
appropriate for the U.S., though it can fit other nations with minor
modifications (I unfortunately couldn't find the original source of the contract
to give credit).


Aaron
----------------------------
                        STANDARD SOCIAL CONTRACT

                Between ___________________________ and

                THE GOVERNMENT OF CENTRAL NORTH AMERICA

WHEREAS: I wish to reside on the Central North American Continent and;
WHEREAS: The Central North American Government controls the area on
which I wish to reside and;
WHEREAS: Tacit and implied contracts are vague and therefore
unenforceable;

THEREFORE, I, THE SIGNER BELOW, agree to the following terms:

SECTION ONE.
        I will surrender a percentage of my property to the Government, such
percentage to be determined by the Government and subject to change at any
time at Government discretion. The amount to be surrendered may be based on
my income, my net worth, the value of my purchases, or any other criteria
the Government may choose.
        To aid the Government in determining the percentage, I will apply for a
Government Identification Number which I will use in all major transactions.

SECTION TWO.
        Upon Government demand, I will surrender my liberty for a period of
time to be determined by the Government, typically no less than two years.
During that time I will serve the Government in any way it chooses, including
military
service in which I may be called upon to sacrifice my life.

SECTION THREE.
        I will limit my behavior when and as demanded by the Government,
including but not limited to the following: I will consume only those drugs
permitted by the Government; I will limit my sexual activities to those
permitted by the Government; I will forsake religious beliefs which conflict
with the Government's determination of propriety.

SECTION FOUR.
        In consideration of the above, the Government will:
        A. Permit me to seek employment, subject to any limits which might
be determined by the Government, such as choice of career or wages I may
accept.
        B. Permit me to reside in the area of North America which it
controls.          
	C. Permit me to speak freely, subject to limits to be
determined from time to time by the President or his authorized
representatives, the Congress and/or the Supreme Court.
        D. Attempt in good faith to protect my life and my claims to any
property it may have allowed me to keep.
        [Note: I may not, however, hold the Government liable,
               or responsible, or accountable in the event it fails to
               successfully protect my safety or my property. The fact
               that the Government may deny me the right, or the means,
               of self-protection places no responsibility whatsoever
               upon the government for any injury or loss I may suffer
               as a result.]

SECTION FIVE:
        The Government may offer various services to me, the nature and
extent of which shall be determined by Government and subject to change at
any time, and for which I may be charged at whatever rate is determined by
Government.

SECTION SIX:
        The Government will determine whether, and when, I may vote for certain
officials, and the relative influence of my vote. The influence of my vote
will normally vary inversely with the total number of voters, and I
understand it typically will be of little or no consequence.
        I agree not to hold any elected Government official liable for acting
against my best interest or for failing to uphold oaths or promises, even if
those promises motivated me to vote for them.

SECTION SEVEN:
        I agree that the Government may hold me fully liable if I fail to abide
by the above terms in their entirety. In the event of such failure on my
part, the Government may confiscate any property that may remain in my
possission, and may imprison me for a period of time to be determined by the
Government. I also agree that the Government may, at its discretion, alter
the terms of this contract at any time.



