I can't see any reason for Digital to sell all the rights to alpha.
That would really be commiting corporate suicide - Digital has no chance as
just another Intel PC manufacturer. Selling all the rights to Intel would
be great from intels point of view - they get out of a protracted lawsuit.
Stop all manufacture of Alpha and bankrupt digital - and then go back to
pinch any other digital patents which weren't in the current dispute.


However I can see a good case for Digital to sell Intel the right to
manufacture Alpha chips. Intel in effect settles the court case and pays
Digital a large sum of money - though probably a lot less than they would
if it had come to court and they had lost. In addition after paying so much
there is at least a fifty-fifty chance that intel will actually start
manufacturing alpha chips.




