Well this is probably a discussion that will never end. Ppl with a reasonable
amount of money have things OK as they can afford education etc. The fact
is that to my knowledge in the states, a lot of families simply can't afford
to educate their children -> their children stay poor -> their children stay
poor etc. There's no real way out of it. I'm quite willing to pay extra
taxes to allow ppl to have the opportunity to educate themselves and gather
money themselves. After all, if it wasn't for a system like that, I would
never have been able to educate myself and thus pay taxes for other ppl
to do so etc.

Now if someone doesn't think this is a good idea and it's OK for rich to
stay rich and poor to stay poor then I can't really comment on that because
the worlds we live in are so different. I know the argument is usually
that "you'll hate it when YOU make lots of money and have to pay high
taxes". Well actually I very much doubt that. In fact I know a lot of ppl
with fairly high salaries who don't really complain about the system at all.
They just accept it knowing how it's helping some other people to study.

This can't be done by free charity as charity never gains enough resources
and political power to do anything worth mentioning to help poverty and free
education. A fact is that ppl are less ready to go out and give money to
some charity than they are to give more of their salaries, if it was
