There is a big difference between communism (marxism) as an idealogy
and communism as a form of politics in countries like russia. Communism's
original idea was to allow everyone a fair chance so the poor don't have
to live in endless poverty. Marxism in it's purest form is pretty utopistic.
In theory it sounds nice and if ppl really were as great as was speculated,
it would probably work OK. Unfortunately or not, the current world situation
doesn't easily support marxism very well. This doesn't mean it's all
totally rubbish and should be completely forgotten. 


