I wrote: "Do you own MicroSoft stock?  What do you do for a living?"

>Do you know what 'poisoning the well' means in the context of logical debate?
>You can drop your attempts to look for ulterior motives and trying the illogical
>ad hominem tactic of discrediting me in that manner.

I have never heard of the expression, "poisoning the well," in that context.
If you can prove my intent, then you are a mind reader.  Otherwise, it is
you who is, "poisoning the well," if I correctly understand the meaning of
that expression.  As a person who earlier criticized someone else for using
an expression about, "getting away with murder," you should not be using such
negative metaphors as, "poisoning the well," yourself.  Just as you earlier
chose to interpret an expression similar to, "getting away with murder," too
literally, if you think that I am interested in doing anything like
harming anyone by poisoning them, then you are wrong.  I think that you
are reading too much into my questions, and I am disappointed that you
did not answer the questions, because I was genuinely curious.

I wrote: "If it were not for the selective enforcement of the antitrust laws
of this country, then MicroSoft itself would soon fall prey to undercutting."
I went on to describe how Japan could subsidize unprofitable industries with
profitable ones with their trillions of dollars of gross domestic product
