>congress or other government officials either.  Microsoft, Netscape, and even
>Japanese companies should all be allowed to compete and succeed or fail on their
>own.

The word, "conspiracy," suggests the image of a group of people involved in
some action which they think is wrong.  If everyone in Japan were to
believe that it is good to give away products for free or at a discounted
price while subsidizing those products with profitable ones, then they
would just be conducting normal business operations, in their view.

