qualms about Japan dominating industries in the United States."

>If they somehow did so (an unlikely scenario, but one I'll stretch and grant you
>for right now that it would be possible) by honest buying and selling and not by
>government force, then that would be perfectly acceptable.  Protectionism is the
>crutch of people who fear they are less competent than others.

You have demonstrated that you are consistent in your beliefs, and we have
nothing more to say to each other, because you have not convinced me, and
I apparently have not convinced you.  If you ever lose whatever job you
currently have because some other company or organization choses to compete
with your company on the basis of how long they can afford to lose money
compared to your company, while subsidizing their losses with other
profitable goods or services, then I hope that you will at least reconsider
your position at that point.

-Ed L



