To some extent bugs and incompatibilities are expected anywhere in the computer
world.  The wise (or 'cynical' :-) ) learn to only upgrade if they really need
performance gain, to avoid a new product until its initial bugs are worked out
in the first couple service packs, and choose what works for long term use.  I
hope more of the mob learns this, and certainly also hope improvement in the
