Aaron Bilger wrote:

<one of a long string of pro free market anti government rants that have
nothing to do with PowerPC Advocacy :-)>

Sometimes people do not think about how we got to our hybrid free market
system. 

In the beginning of time we had a complete free market system. Each
individual gathered their own food and necessities, etc. No government.
Trading and commerce went on but no government existed to provide
services. Some people figured out that if they worked together they
could take all of the food and land from people who had not banded
together. They could also provide assistance when an individual became
unable to hunt. They appointed a leader, probably the best hunter, his
children became the next leaders. These groups worked better than
complete free market systems, so other people formed groups. The best
groups destroyed or assimilated the least effective groups.

 In fact agriculture played a significant part in this development.
Groups that grew their own food could have larger portions of people
involved in warfare and less people involved in the production of food.
These groups could really extinguish the competition. But they needed
more government to monitor food production and control the higher
density population and meet the needs of its workers. And to control the
military. (think of the government as a large corporation that requires
you to follow certain rules at work. If you think of it as oppressive
try working for IBM, EDS or any other large corporation).

As governments grew they invented things like currency to make trading
easier. Prisons and punishments for individuals committing acts that the
government believed inconsistent with its goals. Businesses also got
bigger and more powerful. The government found that having a small
number of large companies that squashed competition and stole inventions
from inventors was inconsistant and ineffective with its goals of having
the best country. So laws were inacted to prevent large companies from
stealing and destroying small companies. (Not to mention that
governments invented Corporations to allow investors to have less
liability so they would be more likely to start companies).

Governments compete with other governments for world domination (well
that is one measure of government success). They do this by having laws
and services that restrict and provide for its citizens (corporate and
real). 

Of course if our federal government ceased to exist tommorrow Mexico and
Canada would happily annex as many states as possible.:-) Michigan,
Texas, California and New York might be able to hold on because of their
large populations but the rest would have to learn to speak spanish or
eat back bacon (eh) ;-). Heck New York would probably annex NJ and
California could grab a few states out west. ;-). Texas believing there
is no better place would just errect huge fences to keep the rest of the
world out. ;-)

To summarize a really short outline of a very complicated theory. Free
Market systems evolve into hybrid free market systems because hybrid
free market systems are better.
