I was in a hurry so I could not go into complete detail and I missed a
few key points. I guess my main point is that a complete free market
does not exist for very long. It is like a vacuum. If you have a
complete free market for a minute, the next minute people will try to
gain an advantage by organizing (creating a proto government or company)
against individuals that have not organized. And then the arms race is
on.

I always try to explain this by going back to our early ancestors
because this is the best way I understand it.

If you look at hunter gathers they only spend about 2 hours a day in
required food, shelter, and etc. activities. The rest of their time is
spent playing or resting. So why did we all agree to spend 12 hours a
day in required activities for living (8 hours working, 1 hour lunch, 2
hours commute, 1 hour eating dinner). Not because we are stupid, well
some would argue this, but because we need to pay taxes to the
organizations that allow us be protected from other large groups. It is
the ultimate protection racket.

This includes corporations that we work for and the government that we
live under. We give our corporations a larger percent of what we produce
than we give the government in taxes. My father in law says for every
dollar that an employee is paid that employee needs to make his company
3 dollars. This is actually a small tax, many large corporations make
much more per dollar than is paid to an employee.

So I was pretty serious but I always smile :-) because the whole
cultural antropology thing is so foriegn to people that I feel like if I
don't smile they won't take the time to understand the real forces going
on.

