>Does anybody have any clue as to how to get the floppy drive working for
>write access on a dec starion 911 system?
>
>
>
  ** I've seen this one numerous times in the Servicenter - Hopefully
this is it. There is a password override jumper on the mainboard of
most Starions. It should only be used to clear the BIOS password.
After that is done you can move the jumper back to the "park" position
(off one pin). If the jumper is left on, the floppy drive stays write
protected. That is the FIRST thing I would check. 
