Please explain your contradiction.  If you say there is no real competition to
the Microsoft operating systems or office, and as you say, no competition means
Microsoft can charge whatever they want, why don't we see them able to charge
whatever they want for their OSes and Office?

>works only when there is actual competition - but when that competition is
>removed, the one who holds all the cards can set whatever price he/she
>wants.  

