>it costs more to develop new technology than many companies would be
>willing to pay were it not for the competition.  After all, would MS have
>even developed IE had it not been for Netscape??

I'm well aware of economic concepts such as monopolistic profits, price
discrimination, decreased efficiency in a monopolistic system, etc.  By the same
token, I'm well aware that predatory pricing is an extraordinarily difficult
tool to wield to obtain and maintain monopolistic power.  If Bill Gates actually
manages to monopolize the browser market so that he can charge whatever he
pleases for MSIE for any length of time, then I'd be amazed at his ability to do
what is essentially impossible without government force.  And in the case that
M$ does drive Netscape and others out and try to charge arbitrarily high prices,
I would offer to join and offer my services to a GNU project to make a free
browser.  I'm curious how many Microsoft-haters here would be willing to
practice what they preach.


Aaron




