>was blue-screened, we've rebooted it now..." ... <sigh>

Ummmm, Rat, you're out to lunch here.  NT was architected by Dave
Cutler.  Prior to coming to Microsoft to work on NT Cutler was the
architect of VMS at Digital.  He left Digital when they shelved a
product he was working on that was to be a follow on to VMS.  When he
went to Microsoft other members of the VMS team also tagged along.
Whatever good you can claim about "the people" who designed VMS also
applies to NT.

