Memnon Emmanuel <memnon@synet.com.gr> writes:
> 	is it possible to connect to CI nodes together without using
> 	a star coupler?
> 	Say i wanted to connect a VAX with a CIXCD to a single 
> 	HSJ40, could I connect the four CI cables crossed ?

  Many of the CI adapters had microcode that would declare a fault if the
receiver didn't detect the transmission. If you've got one of those, I'd
expect to see the system log a failover from the A path to the B path and
then a complete failure.

  DEC never supported this mode of operation (I wanted to try it when I
had an HSC50 and a VAX-11/785).

  Given the large numbers of HSC's being pulled out and dumpstered, you
should be able to get a star coupler pretty inexpensively. If the concern
is the shipping cost or the size of the whole unit, just get the transformer
assembly (SC008, I think). It's a rackmount panel about 12" high. Just be
sure you get enough terminators so you don't have any open TNC connectors
on the star coupler. Running a SC008 "naked" is probably not FCC certified,
so you should make sure you're not interfering with radio/TV if you're in
a residential area.

