Henny Zutt wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> 
> Does anyone know how to connect a VRT19-D3(GDM-1960) 19" monitor to a
> matrox
> millenium video-card in my PC.
> There are 3 BNC connectors on the back of the machine.
> I've searched the "WEB" and found out that you have to use a converter?
> or that you have to modify the cables (soldering) in the back of the
> monitor.
> Does anyone have a complete solution?
> 
> Thanks,
> zutt@pi.net

The first problem is sync on green. Your Matrox outputs separate sync,
NOT the sync on green required by the monitor. Although there are sync
on green adapters out there, they are not standard and therefore may not
work. The other problem is that the VRT19 is a fixed frequency monitor.
If you drive this with a Matrox card, you will only be able to display
hi res graphics (1024x768 and/or 1280x1024). If you want to see all
resolutions and text modes, you will need a different graphics card. Our
Gemini P1 card can output true sync on green, and output the frequency
needed for that monitor.

